[{:db/id -1, :adr/id "2607242500", :adr/title "cloud-itonami-lei-* -- ToSMonitor-LLM/ToSArchiveGovernor actor, round 4: extend from 31 to 41 of ~155 repos, self-paced /loop continuation", :adr/status :accepted, :adr/date "2026-07-24", :adr/doc_type "adr", :adr/source-format "edn", :adr/related ["90-docs/adr/2607241900-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-pilot.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242000-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242300-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round2.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607242400-cloud-itonami-lei-tos-monitor-actor-batch10-round3.edn" "90-docs/adr/2607110300-cloud-itonami-lei-corporate-tos-catalog.edn"], :adr/scope-still-not-fleet-wide "this ADR extends the actor layer to 10 MORE cloud-itonami-lei-* repos (41 of ~155 total after this round). ~114 repos remain untouched, governed solely by ADR-2607110300. This is the first round dispatched automatically by the self-paced /loop set up during round 3 (ADR-2607242400), rather than a fresh owner request -- the owner set up the continuation mechanism explicitly, and this round is that mechanism firing", :adr/batch-companies "cloud-itonami-lei-2138004jbxwwjkiurc57 (Pearson plc, GB), cloud-itonami-lei-2s72qs2uo2oeslg6y829 (Verizon Communications Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-5299008fntq0ldq3uz44 (G8 Education Limited, Australia -- first AU-jurisdiction company in this actor family), cloud-itonami-lei-529900xo0ytookclqb44 (Borussia Dortmund GmbH & Co. KGaA, DE -- first sports-club entity in this actor family), cloud-itonami-lei-549300dovz3edjb7o259 (DXC Technology Company, US-NV), cloud-itonami-lei-549300jz4okehw3dpj59 (Visa Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-549300wr7ix8xe0tbo16 (Kinder Morgan Inc, US-DE), cloud-itonami-lei-96950020qiohaak9v551 (Sopra Steria Group, FR), cloud-itonami-lei-d71fakcblfs2o0rbpg08 (The Williams Companies Inc, US-DE -- first :vendor-terms-and-conditions doc-type company), cloud-itonami-lei-oqsj1du9taoc51a47k68 (Starbucks Corporation, US-WA) -- evenly-spread sample of the remaining pool (124 repos after round 3)", :adr/self-paced-loop-continuation "this round was dispatched automatically when the ScheduleWakeup set up in round 3 fired and re-entered the /loop skill; per that skill's own instructions, firing the loop's stored prompt again means executing one more iteration (this round) and then deciding whether to re-arm another wakeup. No fresh owner message triggered this round -- the owner's round-3 request to 'set up a local loop' is what authorizes this and future rounds to proceed without further per-round requests, consistent with the ADR-2607199960 /loop precedent for this same catalog", :adr/identical-code-per-company "tosmonitor.governor/phase/operation/registry/advisor remain byte-identical across all 41 repos now carrying this actor -- fourth consecutive round with zero further template code changes needed, following round 1's two real fixes", :adr/parallel-subagent-construction "same construction method as round 3 (ADR-2607242400): one independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent per company, self-contained prompt with pre-read real archive metadata, required lint/test bar, and exact git workflow", :adr/test-status-batch10-round4 "each of the 10 repos independently passes its own governor contract (6 HARD checks + high-stakes/never-auto invariant), phase invariants, store parity (MemStore/DatomicStore), and advisor smoke tests before commit", :adr/body "# ADR-2607242500: cloud-itonami-lei-* ToSMonitor round-4 batch-of-10, self-paced /loop continuation\n\n- Status: Accepted (2026-07-24)\n- Related: ADR-2607241900 (pilot); ADR-2607242000/ADR-2607242300/ADR-2607242400 (rounds 1-3);\n  ADR-2607110300 (archive-only design still governing the other ~114 repos).\n\n## Context\n\nDuring round 3 (ADR-2607242400), the owner asked to set up a self-paced continuation\nloop so future batches of 10 would not require a fresh per-round request, mirroring\nADR-2607199960's own `/loop` precedent for this same `cloud-itonami-lei-*` catalog's\ndiscovery/onboarding work. That loop was configured with a ~25-minute fallback\nheartbeat. This ADR records the loop's first automatic re-firing: no new owner\nmessage requested this specific round -- the round-3 request to establish the loop\nis what authorizes it.\n\n## Decision\n\n1. **10 more repos** (41 of ~155 total), evenly sampled from the remaining pool.\n   Two new firsts: G8 Education Limited (Australia, the first AU-jurisdiction company)\n   and Borussia Dortmund (the first sports-club/non-traditional-corporate entity).\n   Also the first real exercise of the `:vendor-terms-and-conditions` doc-type\n   (The Williams Companies) since it was added to `known-doc-types` during round 1's\n   vocabulary-survey fix but not previously hit by a sampled company.\n2. **Same parallel-subagent construction method as round 3.** One company per\n   independently-dispatched Agent-tool subagent, same self-contained prompt pattern,\n   same lint/test bar (0 errors, 25/70 tests), same git workflow (branch, PR via\n   explicit `--head`/`--base`, merge, return to main).\n3. **No further template changes.** Fourth consecutive round with the byte-identical\n   `governor`/`phase`/`operation`/`registry`/`advisor` files requiring zero edits --\n   round 1's two fixes (domain-matching base-domain heuristic, doc-type vocabulary)\n   remain the only code changes across 41 repos and counting.\n4. **Still not fleet-wide.** ~114 `cloud-itonami-lei-*` repos remain untouched,\n   governed solely by ADR-2607110300. The loop re-evaluates after each round whether\n   to continue, per its own dynamic self-pacing logic -- this ADR does not itself\n   commit to any further number of rounds.\n\n## Consequences\n\n- (+) Demonstrates the self-paced `/loop` continuation mechanism working as designed:\n  a round proceeded without a fresh owner request, consistent with what was\n  explicitly asked for in round 3.\n- (+) Further validates the template against two more jurisdiction/entity-type\n  firsts (Australia, a sports club) and one more doc-type (`:vendor-terms-and-\n  conditions`) with zero code changes needed.\n- (-) An unattended, self-paced loop continuing to fire without a human re-confirming\n  scope each time raises the same standing question every prior round's ADR has\n  flagged: whether/when to stop before reaching fleet-wide coverage. This ADR does\n  not resolve that question -- it remains an explicit further decision.\n\n## References\n\n- ADR-2607241900, ADR-2607242000, ADR-2607242300, ADR-2607242400, ADR-2607110300,\n  ADR-2607199960 (the `/loop` continuation precedent)\n- The 10 repos' own `docs/adr/0001-tos-monitor-actor.md` records\n"}]
